## 1.1 Platform Analysis
✅ **Linux Compatible**: This MCP server is written in Python and requires Python >= 3.11 and uv. There are no platform-specific restrictions mentioned, so it can be deployed on Linux (Ubuntu).

## 1.2 Extract Deployment Options

Based on the README, I found the following deployment option:

| Deployment Type | Description | Status |
|----------------|-------------|--------|
| **Local deployment** | Clone the repository and use `uv` to run the server with command: `uv --directory jeb-mcp/src/jeb_mcp run server.py` | ✅ Available |
| Free-installation deployment | No npx/uvx direct installation option provided | ❌ Not available |
| Remote deployment | No cloud-hosted server option provided | ❌ Not available |

## 1.3 Local Deployment Plan

Since only local deployment is available, I'll follow this plan:
1. Clone the repository using git
2. Use uv to run the MCP server from the `jeb-mcp/src/jeb_mcp` directory

