## 1.1 Platform Analysis

This is a **Python-based MCP server** that requires Python 3.10+ and the FastMCP library. The README shows configuration examples for Mac OS, Windows, and Linux (CLine config uses bash with Linux paths). Since this is a Python project with no platform-specific restrictions, **it can be deployed on Linux (Ubuntu)**. ✅

## 1.2 Deployment Options Extraction

Based on the README, I've identified the following deployment options:

| Option | Type | Status |
|--------|------|--------|
| Smithery CLI installation (npx @smithery/cli) | Free-installation | **[PROHIBITED]** |
| Manual local installation (git clone + pip install) | Local deployment | ✅ Available |
| Remote cloud deployment | Remote deployment | ❌ Not provided |

